   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A degree 2 polynomial needs the values through order 2: \\( f(-1) = 2 \\), \\( f'(-1) = 0 \\), \\( f''(-1) = 6 \\). The value of order 3 is not used.",
         "mathjson": 6
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Divide each by the matching factorial: \\( \\frac{2}{0!} = 2 \\), \\( \\frac{0}{1!} = 0 \\), \\( \\frac{6}{2!} = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Attach \\( (x + 1)^{k} \\) to the coefficient of order \\( k \\): \\( P(x) = 2 + 3(x + 1)^{2} \\).",
